\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every Artin algebra $A$, is
\[
\sup\{\operatorname{pd}_A(M): M\text{ is finitely generated and }\operatorname{pd}_A(M)<\infty\}
\]
finite?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every Artin algebra $A$, are the finite projective dimensions $\operatorname{pd}_A(M)$ of its finitely generated modules $M$ bounded above?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2005/06}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/An-algebra-of-infinite-little-finitistic-dimension-September-23-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

